5

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕NC'⍞_'
¯1

      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #24, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ ⎕NC of a system FUNCTION name (⎕EA, ⎕FX, ...) gave ¯1 (invalid)
      ⍝ instead of 6, because Workspace::get_quad() returns a function
      ⍝ token (not a Symbol) for these, and get_NC() only ever checked
      ⍝ the Symbol/TC_SYMBOL path. Per ISO/IEC 13751 11.5.2, 5=system
      ⍝ variable, 6=system function.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕NC of GNU APL names/classes differs
      ⎕NC 3 3⍴'⎕EA⎕IO⎕KZ'
6 5 ¯1

      ⎕NC 3⍴'⎕FX'
6

      ⎕NC 4⍴'⎕FFT'
6

      ⍝ prefix-tolerance must still be rejected for functions too
      ⍝ (same rule as the existing '⎕XX' case above, for variables)
      ⍝
      ⎕NC 7⍴'⎕FFTxyz'
¯1

      ⍝ Bugs28 #48 regression: ⎕NC of a NESTED vector of names (see the
      ⍝ matching, more detailed comment in testcases/Quad_EX.tc) had
      ⍝ the same bug as ⎕EX -- one shared root cause
      ⍝ (QuadFunction.cc's new quad_EX_NC_names()).
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ZZ48NA←1 ⋄ ZZ48NB←2
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ structured variables are a GNU APL extension; ⎕NC of GNU APL names/classes differs
      ⎕NC 'ZZ48NA' 'ZZ48NB'
2 2

      ⎕NC 'ZZ48NA' 'ZZ48NOSUCH'
2 0

      )ERASE ZZ48NA ZZ48NB

      ⍝ Bugs28 #54 regression: ⎕NC of an existing MEMBER of a
      ⍝ structured variable (e.g. S.a) gave ¯1 ("invalid name") --
      ⍝ get_NC() had no member (.) handling at all, looked up the
      ⍝ WHOLE string "S.a" as one symbol name (never found, since '.'
      ⍝ is not a valid symbol character), and fell through to the
      ⍝ "user-defined name" path's per-char validation, which rejects
      ⍝ the '.'. doc/apl.texi says the usual rules for normal
      ⍝ variables apply to members: an existing member is a variable
      ⍝ (2), a nonexistent member of an otherwise-existing structured
      ⍝ variable is simply unused (0, same as any other undefined
      ⍝ name). Fixed by detecting the '.' and reusing
      ⍝ try_existing_member() (Bugs28 #53) to check without throwing.
      ⍝
      ZZ54S.a←1
      ⎕NC 'ZZ54S.a'
2

      ⎕NC 'ZZ54S'
2

      ⎕NC 'ZZ54S.zz'
0

      ⍝ control: a nonexistent base variable is also just unused
      ⍝
      ⎕NC 'ZZ54NOSUCH.a'
0

      ⍝ control: ⎕EX already correctly treated the member as a name
      ⍝
      ⎕EX 'ZZ54S.a'
1

      ⎕NC 'ZZ54S.a'
0

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #88): ⎕NC of a character matrix B used to
      ⍝ give a scalar Z (via "var_count > 1", false for a 1- or 0-row
      ⍝ matrix) instead of a vector sized to B's row count (ISO 13751:
      ⍝ ⍴Z ←→ ↑⍴B) -- a scalar Z whose single cell is then never
      ⍝ written (the result loop runs 0 or 1 times either way) is an
      ⍝ incomplete value.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⍴⎕NC 1 1⍴'A'
1

      ⍴⎕NC 0 3⍴'A'
0

      ⍝ ==================================


